From 62b46b73374cc636e3e0aeb0d492ee077cc2210b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-bst <zeqing.xu@bluestacks.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:20:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [A16] Report SELinux disabled to Android userspace

Source: A13 external/selinux d42add96533decac77101c314e5abceae20070d7.

Purpose: preserve the App Player compatibility contract where Android callers skip SELinux context and restorecon paths while init keeps the kernel in permissive mode.

Adaptation: retain upstream host libselinux detection and return disabled only for Android builds, limiting the behavior change to the guest product.

Necessity: AOSP16 omitted this authority patch; installd, cmd, restorecon, and libselinux Android helpers otherwise take a different path from A13.

Performance: avoids restorecon/context work and therefore cannot add boot cost.

Security: intentionally suppresses Android userspace SELinux handling; this is a broad defense-in-depth reduction inherited from A13 and requires runtime boot validation.

Validation: target libselinux, init, and installd build passed; host libselinux_test passed 12/12 for 32/64; target 32/64 disassembly independently confirms a zero return.
---
 libselinux/src/enabled.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libselinux/src/enabled.c b/libselinux/src/enabled.c
index fefb0bd9..168f604a 100644
--- a/libselinux/src/enabled.c
+++ b/libselinux/src/enabled.c
@@ -10,12 +10,17 @@
 
 int is_selinux_enabled(void)
 {
-	/* init_selinuxmnt() gets called before this function. We
- 	 * will assume that if a selinux file system is mounted, then
- 	 * selinux is enabled. */
+	/*
+	 * BlueStacks App Player intentionally exposes SELinux as disabled to
+	 * Android userspace. The kernel remains permissive, while callers such as
+	 * installd and restorecon follow the A13 compatibility path.
+	 */
 #ifdef ANDROID
-	return (selinux_mnt ? 1 : 0);
+	return 0;
 #else
+	/* init_selinuxmnt() gets called before this function. We
+	 * will assume that if a selinux file system is mounted, then
+	 * selinux is enabled. */
 	return (selinux_mnt && has_selinux_config);
 #endif
 }
@@ -53,4 +58,3 @@ int is_selinux_mls_enabled(void)
 
 	return enabled;
 }
-
